  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while Image (ResNet50, single profile) achieves only 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether using multiple profiles with aggregation (avgpool) improves upon the single-profile RNA baseline. This experiment (config_002) isolates the effect of multiprofile + avgpool aggregation while keeping the same PCA n2000 encoder as config_001, making it a clean single-variable comparison. It is the best next step because it tests a fundamental architectural choice (single vs. multiprofile) for the clearly dominant modality; if multiprofile helps, it validates the aggregation pathway and justifies investing remaining budget in transformer aggregation and multimodal multiprofile variants, while if it doesn't help, it eliminates ~15 configurations and redirects budget toward encoder improvements (scvi/scgpt) or better image encoders (ViT-L)."
}

